**What changed and why:**

| Problem | Fix |
|---------|-----|
| `for (Opportunity opp : Trigger.new)` doesn't compile in a class file | Accept `List<sObject>` parameters from the trigger; cast individual records with `(Opportunity) so` |
| `Trigger.new` / `Trigger.old` accessed directly in the class | Passed explicitly as arguments from the trigger file (where the compiler knows the SObject type) |
| `Trigger.isInsert` / `.isUpdate` / `.isDelete` / `.isUndelete` | Still accessible in a class called from a trigger (no compiler error was raised for these), so they remain in the handler |
| Recursion from `AccountTrigger`'s `update opps` | Static `isRecursing` flag set before the account `update`, cleared in `finally` |
| Correctness across multiple DML statements | Full recalculation from a SOQL query each time (sees uncommitted changes in the same transaction) |
| 200-record bulk loads | Single SOQL + single `update` statement |

